WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.020
Acting is a serious craft.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:06.440
Long before the cameras start rolling, most
great actors prepare for their roles by memorizing

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:10.620
lines and conducting exhaustive research,
while striving to perfect every mannerism

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.260
of the subject.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.780
Sometimes, though, this extensive preparation
comes at a cost.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.020
Which actors went to surprising extremes and
almost died preparing for their roles?

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.520
Was the price they paid really worth it?

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.080
We'll let you be the judge.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:24.800
Matthew McConaughey

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.840
Following a string of fluffy rom-coms in the
late 2000s, it was pretty hard to take Matthew

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.960
McConaughey seriously.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.620
"Dazed and confused is the one thing that
was passable... after that"

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.880
"Aw, thanks man, that actually launched my
career."

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:39.440
"After that, everything else was awful."

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.420
McConaughey managed to reignite his career
with a run of critically acclaimed movies

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:47.420
which culminated in an Oscar win for his star
turn in Dallas Buyers Club.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.940
However, it turns out that the actor's Oscar
win very nearly cost him his sight.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:57.659
After dropping 38 pounds to play someone suffering
from AIDS, McConaughey started experiencing

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.920
problems with his vision and consulted doctors
for medical help.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.180
Fortunately, the effects weren't permanent,
although McConaughey did reveal to Metro that

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.000
the extreme stress he put his body through
was still affecting his sight over a year

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.500
later.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:14.120
If McConaughey had continued down the dangerous
path of self-imposed starvation, it's likely

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.440
that the effects could have been even more
dangerous.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:17.820
Johnny Depp

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.080
Fear &amp; Loathing in Las Vegas represents an
interesting turning point in Johnny Depp's

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:26.540
career, and not just because he could have
exploded, literally, at any point.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:31.140
Months before filming began, author Hunter
S. Thompson allowed Depp to live in his basement

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:32.560
to prepare for the adaptation.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.100
During his time in the house, Depp taped conversations,
smoked cigarettes, and even wore Thompson's

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:37.780
old clothes.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.500
The star has since shared fond memories of
this time.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:47.869
"As he got closer I realized he had a three-foot
cattle prod in his left hand, and a taser

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:48.960
in his right hand."

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.340
Yeah, hee hee, just tryin' to make friends."

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.560
However, Thompson's act of generosity could
have led to Depp's untimely death.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:02:00.100
After a few days, Depp discovered something
terrifying: the cigarettes he'd been smoking

00:02:00.109 --> 00:02:04.229
in the basement could have blown the house
sky high, thanks to the gunpowder keg stored

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:06.040
down in the basement beside him.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.420
"This is a very ominous assignment, with overtones
of extreme personal danger.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.280
Occupational journalism man.

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.360
This is important Goddammit!"

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.920
Daniel Day-Lewis

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:20.880
Though now retired, Daniel Day-Lewis is the
poster child for modern method acting, taking

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:26.150
extreme measures to prepare for every movie
he stars in, from refusing to leave his wheelchair

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:30.020
while filming My Left Foot, to living on prison
rations for In The Name Of The Father?

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.650
Surprisingly, the most dangerous preparation
that Day-Lewis made for a role actually sounds

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.620
relatively safe.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:39.900
While playing the part of Bill the Butcher
in Martin Scorsese's Gangs of New York, Lewis

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.060
simply refused to wear a warm coat while walking
around the wintry streets of New York.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:45.120
Why?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.440
The poor 19th century character he was playing
would have never owned such a luxury.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:53.580
Unsurprisingly, the threadbare coat he sported
didn't do much to keep him warm, and Lewis

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.300
caught pneumonia.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:59.130
He even initially refused treatment because
the medicine wouldn't have been period appropriate.

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.620
Talk about committing to a role.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.700
"This is a night for Americans!"

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.460
Martin Lawrence

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.940
Comedians always need to have a joke or two
up their sleeve, but the real challenge of

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.400
comedy lies in the physicality of the performance.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.160
Martin Lawrence learned this lesson all too
well following his part in Big Momma's House.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:23.960
To prepare for the latex fat suit that the
role of Big Momma would require him to wear,

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:28.880
Lawrence decided to jog wearing heavy clothing
and a plastic suit in 100-degree heat.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:33.540
At the end of his ill-fated run, Lawrence
collapsed due to extreme dehydration and heat

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.040
exhaustion.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.720
When he first arrived at the hospital, his
body temperature hit a startling 107 degrees

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.760
and a ventilator was required to help him
breathe after he slipped into a coma that

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:43.660
lasted for three days.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:47.760
Lawrence's attending physicians initially
feared that there might be permanent brain

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.740
damage, but Lawrence would make a full recovery.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.240
"Is that all you got?

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.400
Well ya'll better get ready to sit down cause
you ain't gonna last long once we get all

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:56.900
in here.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.400
Ain't that right?"

00:03:58.880 --> 00:03:59.440
Matt Damon

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:05.360
For his role in the 1996 movie Courage Under
Fire, Matt Damon took desperate measures and

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:09.920
underwent an extreme diet to play a former
soldier traumatized by the effects of war.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.460
Damon's character had become addicted to heroin,
so Damon lost 40 pounds in order to portray

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.260
the toll that would take on the human body.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.640
Unfortunately for Damon, his strict diet took
a toll on his health in real life, too.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.940
For months after filming ended, the star had
to remain under strict medical supervision

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.400
and take medication for the damage he'd inflicted
on his adrenal gland.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:32.580
The young actor later revealed in an Reddit
AMA that he regretted his methods and was

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:36.720
even told by a doctor that undergoing the
unsupervised diet could have permanently shrunk

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.680
his heart if he'd continued much longer.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.040
Ashton Kutcher

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:44.800
Eager to prove himself as a serious actor,
Ashton Kutcher took on the role of American

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.460
entrepreneur Steve Jobs in the 2013 bio-pic,
Jobs.

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:52.430
Speaking after the premiere screening at Sundance,
Kutcher told the audience he felt close to

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.750
the film's subject.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:57.340
To prepare for this part, Kutcher grew his
hair long and spent hours studying tapes of

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:00.900
the Apple CEO in action to help him replicate
his various mannerisms.

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:02.700
It turns out that wasn't enough.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:07.940
Before filming, Kutcher also decided to replicate
his subject's diet and only ate fruit, nuts,

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:08.440
and seeds.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.360
While this might sound healthy in theory,
Kutcher wound up hospitalized for pancreatitis

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.360
just a few days before shooting began.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:19.540
Kutcher's not exaggerating when he says the
experience was absolutely terrifying, but

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.400
luckily, the actor made a full recovery.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.100
Hilary Swank

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.259
It's not unusual for actors working on fight
movies to suffer from painful injuries, but

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:32.039
Hilary Swank endured a more dangerous wound
than most while preparing for Million Dollar

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.520
Baby—and it all started with a simple blister.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:39.160
As a result of having to pivot on her feet
constantly during training, Swank developed

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:42.960
a blister on her right foot which she claimed
was the size of her palm.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.750
During an interview with correspondent Mike
Wallace for 60 Minutes, Swank explained how

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:51.340
it became impossible for her to train or walk
on the blister, so she popped it herself,

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.240
which led to a dangerous staph infection that
could have been fatal if left untreated.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.220
"Don't come crying to me if you get hurt,
alrighty?"

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:00.240
"We got a deal."

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:01.680
Robert De Niro

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.340
There's more where that came from when it
comes to boxing movies that injured their

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:05.840
stars.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.620
Now regarded as a masterpiece of filmmaking
and one of Martin Scorsese's best movies,

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.880
Raging Bull suffered a number of setbacks
during production that could have knocked

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.100
the film out of the running before it even
got started.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:20.840
Actor Robert De Niro transformed himself for
the role of Jake La Motta, training for nearly

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:23.180
a year to embody the part of a real-life boxer.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.860
During training, he boxed around 1,000 rounds
in a gym to add 20 pounds of muscle to his

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:31.060
frame, and even broke his mentor's rib along
the way.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:36.120
However, when production in LA was completed,
De Niro was sent to Europe on an eating spree,

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.020
as the role required him to gain weight so
he could play La Motta on the decline too.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:44.700
After gaining 60 pounds over a period of four
months, De Niro returned to New York to finish

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.300
filming, but the weight gain came at a price.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:52.000
After his star showed signs of struggling
with his posture, breathing and even talking,

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:56.540
Scorsese decided to temporarily halt production,
as he believed De Niro might be at risk of

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:57.160
a heart attack.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.540
"You want your steak?"

00:06:58.540 --> 00:06:59.040
Bring it over.

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:01.040
Bring it over.

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:04.640
It's like a piece of charcoal, bring it over
here!"

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:05.900
"You want your steak?"

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:06.600
"Yeah!"

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:07.720
Christian Bale

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:12.360
Brad Anderson's disturbing thriller was lauded
for its fascinating insight into paranoia

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:16.479
and delusion, but ultimately, The Machinist
will always be remembered most vividly for

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:18.660
Christian Bale's jaw-dropping performance.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:23.580
To play the part of a man suffering from insomnia
and other serious psychological problems,

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:28.460
Christian Bale dropped over 60 pounds, reducing
his body mass to just 120 pounds.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:33.520
During a Reddit AMA, co-star Michael Ironside
revealed an even more disturbing insight into

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:38.060
the dangerous extremes that Bale's diet took,
explaining how starvation had ravaged his

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:38.880
body, saying,

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.720
"[Chris] said, 'Can you look at this?'

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:45.000
And he turned and dropped his overalls [...] and
the muscles in his ass had literally dropped

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.460
out of the sockets of his hips."

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:51.120
As if that wasn't dangerous enough, Bale only
had six weeks to regain his normal weight

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:55.639
before putting on the cape and cowl for his
Batman Begins screen test, and then just five

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.720
months more to develop a physique worthy of
the caped crusader.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:02.160
According to Ironside though, he didn't seem
to have much trouble managing it.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:10.480
"It's not who I am underneath, but what I
do that defines me."

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:11.600
Thanks for watching!

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.860
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.400
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

